# ── Shared per-version OS base images (PB-273/PB-265, 2026-08-15) ───────────
# Real qcow2 disk images (hundreds of MB+), fetched onto the Fedora host by
# playbook_273_fetch_os_image.yml and read by every VM-creation playbook for
# that Ecosystem version. Lives inside the Forge tree by design (Architect
# request: one unified, version-pinned location per Ecosystem version), but
# is host-local build output, not source -- never committed to git.
Infra/OSImage/

# ── Benchmark / profiling artefacts ──────────────────────────────────────────
criterion/
flamegraph.svg
perf.data
perf.data.old

# ── Coverage ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
lcov.info
coverage/
tarpaulin-report.html

# ── IsimudEngine generated reports (regenerated every run — not source) ──
# `docs/SHEDU/*` (not `docs/SHEDU/`) is deliberate: a directory-level
# pattern with a trailing slash prunes the whole directory from
# traversal, so a later per-file negation would be silently never
# evaluated (confirmed live via `git check-ignore -v` -- both a generated
# report AND an intended exception matched the same directory rule). The
# `*` form still ignores every file by default but keeps per-file
# negation usable if a future exception is ever needed again.
#
# 2026-08-15 doc taxonomy reorg: the 5 authored-content files that used
# to live under docs/SHEDU/ (and needed the negation exceptions this
# comment used to describe) moved to their real category homes
# (docs/16_runbooks/, docs/13_changelog/, docs/18_security/) -- none of
# which sit under any blanket ignore, so no exception is needed for them
# anymore. docs/SHEDU/ itself remains live and ignored: dozens of
# playbooks and anu-governor.toml's report_dir/chronicle_dir still write
# real run-output there.
docs/SHEDU/*

# ── Real key/passport material — never committed, real infra, real risk ──
# Found live 2026-08-26: a `git add -A` on a real bare-metal checkout
# staged all 5 Gilgamesh Shamir shares, the reconstructed master key
# file, and both Architect passports, together, in one commit -- nothing
# here had ever been declared ignored. Splitting a secret into N shares
# only protects it if the shares never end up back in one place; a git
# repo (especially once pushed anywhere) is exactly one place.
**/architect-key-SHARE-*-of-*.json
**/Gilgamesh_MasterKy.json
**/gilgamesh-ledger-record-*.json
**/architect-PASSPORT*.json
**/sargon-PASSPORT*.json
**/sargon_vault/*.json
**/Gilgamesh_Sec*/
**/Gligamesh_*Splits*/
